xdebug 3.1.6 declares xdebug_develop_minit() with an empty parameter list
while its definition takes INIT_FUNC_ARGS. On PHP 8.x INIT_FUNC_ARGS_PASSTHRU
expands to `type, module_number`, so the call in xdebug.c fails with
"too many arguments to function call, expected 0, have 2".

3.1.6 is the only xdebug line that still supports PHP 7.4 (3.2+ require 8.0),
so the declaration is corrected here. The sibling hooks (gcstats, debugger,
profiler) genuinely take no arguments in both declaration and definition and
are left alone.

--- a/src/develop/develop.h
+++ b/src/develop/develop.h
@@ -67,7 +67,7 @@
 void xdebug_init_develop_globals(xdebug_develop_globals_t *xg);
 void xdebug_deinit_develop_globals(xdebug_develop_globals_t *xg);
 
-void xdebug_develop_minit();
+void xdebug_develop_minit(INIT_FUNC_ARGS);
 void xdebug_develop_mshutdown();
 void xdebug_develop_rinit();
 void xdebug_develop_post_deactivate();
